"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3416794260","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111093#issuecomment-3416794260","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111093","id":3416794260,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LqCSU","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T19:17:44Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T19:40:56Z","body":"I'm currently running into this issue with rigid bodies overlapping when using Jolt Physics in 2D (with this PR):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cf2d3bc3-1a2a-4b89-9f78-8fc59a1d6e0e\r\n\r\nI understand that the penetration will happen without CCD enabled, but I don't understand why it doesn't depenetrate afterwards. This doesn't happen with GodotPhysics2D. I'm not sure how to solve this.\r\n\r\n(Test project: [2D Physics Tests](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/2d/physics_tests) > Functional Tests > Box Pyramid.)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3416794260/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3747723892","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111093#issuecomment-3747723892","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111093","id":3747723892,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fYbp0","user":{"login":"LeaoLuciano","id":56130740,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTMwNzQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56130740?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano","html_url":"https://github.com/LeaoLuciano","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-14T04:57:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-14T04:57:28Z","body":"> I'm currently running into this issue with rigid bodies overlapping when using Jolt Physics in 2D (with this PR):\r\n> Screencast.From.2025-10-17.21-12-40.mp4\r\n> \r\n> I understand that the penetration will happen without CCD enabled, but I don't understand why it doesn't depenetrate afterwards. This doesn't happen with GodotPhysics2D. I'm not sure how to solve this.\r\n> \r\n> (Test project: [2D Physics Tests](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/2d/physics_tests) > Functional Tests > Box Pyramid.)\r\n\r\nI changed ```#define SIZE2TO3(m_size2) (SCALE_2D_TO_3D * Vector3(m_size2.x, m_size2.y, 5))``` to ```#define SIZE2TO3(m_size2) (SCALE_2D_TO_3D * Vector3(m_size2.x, m_size2.y, 100.0))``` and it worked:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad37432b-0e0e-4e88-8d0e-e7cb1045a97c\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3747723892/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3937494765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111093#issuecomment-3937494765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111093","id":3937494765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qsWbt","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T22:42:07Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T22:42:07Z","body":"Thanks for that @LeaoLuciano!\r\n\r\nI updated the PR. I also added `JoltBody::has_one_way_collision_shapes()` to optimize contact filtering, and I added support for custom one-way collision direction, which allowed to make this PR work without introducing a strange default value in 3D (namely `Vector2.DOWN` is `(0, 1)`, and our embedding is mapping `(x, y)` to `(x, y, 0)`, but `Vector3.DOWN` is `(0, -1, 0)`, so without custom one-way collision direction we would have had to make the default 3D one-way collision direction `Vector3.UP`).\r\n\r\nThe main thing left to do is one-way collisions for character bodies (as in the 2D platformer demo) in Jolt, probably around `JoltPhysicsDirectSpaceState3D::_body_motion_recover`, `JoltPhysicsDirectSpaceState3D::_cast_motion_impl`, and `JoltPhysicsDirectSpaceState3D::_body_motion_collide`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3937494765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3938722218","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111093#issuecomment-3938722218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111093","id":3938722218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qxCGq","user":{"login":"LeaoLuciano","id":56130740,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTMwNzQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56130740?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano","html_url":"https://github.com/LeaoLuciano","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeaoLuciano/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T12:40:15Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T12:40:15Z","body":"@rburing I was tweaking this PR last week and found a few problems:\r\n - Scaled StaticBodies collisions weren't working because using just angles and origins to make Transform3Ds isn't enough\r\n - Groove joints weren't affected by rotations \r\n - Groove joints were too soft\r\n - Damped spring joints weren't working at all\r\n\r\nI've fixed the first 2 problems in my branch (https://github.com/LeaoLuciano/godot/tree/physics_server_2d_in_3d), but I got stuck on the 3rd because I couldn't find a way to adjust the softness using 6DOF joints.\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3938722218/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]